<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edward Whymper</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1840–1911</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edward Whymper was an English mountaineer, engraver and author. On 14 July 1865 he led the first ascent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matterhorn">Matterhorn</a>, but four of his party were killed on the descent when a rope broke, a disaster that made the climb famous. His book Scrambles amongst the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> popularised Alpine climbing, and he later explored the Andes of Ecuador and the Canadian Rockies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edward-whymper.jpg" alt="Edward Whymper" width="240" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User Primetime on en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edward_Whymper.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
